{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they shall bear them.</b> They shall bear the guilt upon themselves <b>when they eat their holy things</b> — that were set apart for the designation of terumah, and became sanctified and forbidden to them; and Onkelos, who rendered ״בְּמֵיכָלְהוֹן בְּסוֹאֲבָא״ — he did not translate it for this purpose." "<b>And they shall bear them.</b> This is one of three instances of אֶת that Rabbi Yishmael would expound in the Torah as speaking of the person himself; likewise ״בְּיוֹם מְלֹאת יְמֵי נִזְרוֹ יָבִיא אֹתוֹ״ (Numbers 6) — he brings himself; and likewise ״וַיִּקְבֹּר אֹתוֹ בַגַּי״ (Deuteronomy 34) — he buried himself; so it is expounded in Sifrei."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:45.630730248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}